@extends('layouts/marketing')

<script server>
useSeoMeta({
  title: 'loghq vs Airbrake - loghq',
  description: 'How loghq, an open-source error tracker you self-host on Postgres, compares to Airbrake, one of the original error trackers.',
  ogImage: 'https://loghq.org/og.png',
})
useHead({ link: [{ rel: 'canonical', href: 'https://loghq.org/compare/airbrake' }] })

// Breadcrumb trail. One array drives two consumers — the rendered list in
// the Breadcrumbs partial and the BreadcrumbList JSON-LD below — so the
// markup and the structured data cannot disagree. The last crumb has no
// href or url: it is this page.
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/', url: 'https://loghq.org/' },
  { label: 'Compare', href: '/compare', url: 'https://loghq.org/compare' },
  { label: 'Airbrake' },
]
</script>


@section('content')
@structuredData({
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: crumbs.map((c, i) => ({ '@type': 'ListItem', position: i + 1, name: c.label, item: c.url })),
})

@include('Breadcrumbs')

<section class="feat-hero shell">
  <span class="kicker">Compare</span>
  <h1>loghq vs Airbrake</h1>
  <p>Airbrake is one of the original error trackers, now a closed-source SaaS with error monitoring and light performance features. The capture-and-triage loop it made familiar is exactly what loghq provides, as an open project you can run on your own Postgres instead of a hosted-only account.</p>
  <div class="hero-actions">
    <StxLink class="btn primary" to="/register">Get started</StxLink>
    <StxLink class="btn ghost" to="/compare">All alternatives</StxLink>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="reveal section shell" aria-labelledby="table-heading">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2 id="table-heading" class="section-title">loghq and Airbrake, side by side</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="cmp cmp-hl">
  <div class="cmp-cell">Capability</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell bg-accent-soft">loghq</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">Airbrake</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">What it is</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost bg-accent-soft">Focused error and crash tracking</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">Error and performance monitoring</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">Open source</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost bg-accent-soft">Yes, open source</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">No</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">Self-host / data ownership</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost bg-accent-soft">Yes, your own Postgres</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">No, SaaS only</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">Pricing model</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost bg-accent-soft">Free self-hosted, usage-based hosted</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">Event-volume based</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">Error grouping</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost bg-accent-soft">Automatic fingerprinting</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">Yes</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">Source maps and stack traces</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost bg-accent-soft">Full source-mapped traces</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">Yes</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">Releases and environments</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost bg-accent-soft">Built in</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">Yes, deploy tracking</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">Alerting</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost bg-accent-soft">New and spiking issues</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">Yes</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-dim">Data retention</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell cmp-ghost bg-accent-soft">Yours to set when self-hosted</div>
  <div class="cmp-cell">Plan-based</div>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-subtle text-[0.86rem] leading-[1.55]">Where Airbrake still leads: it is a long-established tool with deep, mature SDKs for Ruby and other classic server stacks.</p>
</section>

<section class="reveal section shell" aria-labelledby="why-heading">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2 id="why-heading" class="section-title">Why teams pick loghq</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="flow">
    <div class="flow-step">
      <span class="flow-num">01</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Own your data</h3>
        <p>Airbrake is SaaS only. loghq self-hosts on your own Postgres, keeping error payloads on your infrastructure.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flow-step">
      <span class="flow-num">02</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Open source</h3>
        <p>loghq is open and self-hostable, so ingestion and grouping are transparent rather than a hosted black box.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flow-step">
      <span class="flow-num">03</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Predictable cost</h3>
        <p>Event-volume billing rises with incidents and traffic. Self-hosted loghq breaks that link and costs nothing to run yourself.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="reveal section shell" aria-label="Fair comparison">
  <div class="chips">
    <div class="chip">
      <h3>Credit where it is due</h3>
      <p>Airbrake has a long track record and battle-tested SDKs, especially in the Ruby world. loghq is the newer, open, self-hostable option covering the same essentials.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="chip">
      <h3>What loghq is</h3>
      <p>Open-source error and crash tracking you can run on your own Postgres, or use on a hosted tier. Automatic capture, fingerprint grouping, source-mapped traces, releases, and alerts, without the rest of an observability suite.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="reveal section shell" aria-labelledby="related-heading">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2 id="related-heading" class="section-title">More comparisons</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="related">
    <StxLink to="/compare/rollbar">
      <div class="r-name">loghq vs Rollbar</div>
      <div class="r-desc">A closed-source SaaS error tracker.</div>
    </StxLink>
    <StxLink to="/compare/honeybadger">
      <div class="r-name">loghq vs Honeybadger</div>
      <div class="r-desc">Errors plus uptime and cron monitoring.</div>
    </StxLink>
    <StxLink to="/compare/sentry">
      <div class="r-name">loghq vs Sentry</div>
      <div class="r-desc">The incumbent error platform, compared.</div>
    </StxLink>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="reveal section shell" aria-label="Get started">
  <div class="cta-band">
    <h2>Own your error tracking.</h2>
    <div class="cta-actions">
      <StxLink class="btn primary" to="/register">Get started</StxLink>
      <StxLink class="btn ghost" to="/features/self-host">Read about self-hosting</StxLink>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
@endsection
